\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Negative</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> With Count Nouns</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> How many books? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"so many books<br />a lot of books\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"not many books\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> With Non-count Nouns</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> How much water? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"so much water<br />a lot of water\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"not much water\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  You use <span class=\"strong\">some</span> with count nouns (in the singular) or with non-count nouns (in the plural) to talk about the number of items. <br /> You use <span class=\"strong\">many</span> with count nouns to talk about the number of items. <br /> You use <span class=\"strong\">much</span> with non-count nouns to talk about the amount or quantity of an item. <br /> You use <span class=\"strong\">a lot of</span> with count and non-count nouns. <br /> Note: You use <span class=\"strong\">many</span> and <span class=\"strong\">much</span> with <span class=\"strong\">so</span> in statements, or use <span class=\"strong\">a lot of</span> instead."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn1le05ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read the short dialogue with a partner. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " Now, write a dialogue. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " You are at a cafe.  Offer your partner a dessert and drink. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Accept or refuse the offer. 